otor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T20:53:50-08:00","id":1432371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1333493-rules-for-poetry-duel-with-focus-on-east-asian-literature?p=1430909#post1430909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, this is <i>fascinating</i>! I really like that you allow the use of unusual skills like Animal Ken during the Middle phase of poem composition, that rule opens up a lot of interesting possibilities. <a href=\"https://emojipedia.org/thinking-face/#:~:text=May%20be%20paired%20with%20%F0%9F%92%AD,to%20Emoji%201.0%20in%202015.\" target=\"_blank\">\ud83e\udd14</a> I definitely want to find a way to use this in the next game I run.<br /> <br /> I kind of wonder: could I get your permission to include a link to this in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\">Motor City Breakdown</a> setting, to simulate rap battles and freestyling? I bet these rules could also be useful in Viking chronicles where <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flyting#\" target=\"_blank\">flyting</a> happens, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Feel free to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}